> This document outlines the responsibilities, qualifications, and expectations for the Senior Software Engineer role at NexaTech Solutions. We are looking for passionate and talented engineers to join our team and help us build the future of business intelligence.

## Job Description: Senior Software Engineer

**Location:** Austin, TX; Berlin, Germany; or Remote
**Department:** Engineering & Product Development
**Reports to:** Engineering Manager

### About NexaTech Solutions

NexaTech Solutions is a fast-growing enterprise software company specializing in cloud-based business intelligence and data analytics. Our mission is to empower organizations with intelligent, scalable, and intuitive solutions that transform data into actionable insights. We are a team of innovators, collaborators, and problem-solvers, and we are looking for talented individuals to join us on our journey.

### The Role

As a Senior Software Engineer, you will be a key member of our backend engineering team, responsible for designing, building, and maintaining the core services that power our flagship NexaInsight Platform. You will work in a fast-paced, agile environment, collaborating with product managers, designers, and other engineers to deliver high-quality, scalable, and secure software.

### Responsibilities

*   Design, develop, and maintain robust and scalable backend services and APIs.
*   Write clean, maintainable, and well-tested code in Python, Go, and/or Node.js.
*   Collaborate with cross-functional teams to define, design, and ship new features.
*   Mentor junior engineers and contribute to a culture of technical excellence.
*   Participate in code reviews to ensure code quality and distribute knowledge.
*   Troubleshoot and resolve production issues.
*   Contribute to the continuous improvement of our engineering processes and standards.

### Qualifications

*   5+ years of professional software development experience.
*   Strong proficiency in at least one of our backend languages: Python, Go, or Node.js.
*   Experience with microservices architecture and building RESTful APIs.
*   Experience with cloud platforms (AWS preferred) and containerization technologies (Docker, Kubernetes).
*   Solid understanding of data structures, algorithms, and software design principles.
*   Experience with relational and NoSQL databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MongoDB).
*   Excellent problem-solving and communication skills.
*   Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a related field, or equivalent experience.

### Preferred Qualifications

*   Experience with data-intensive applications or business intelligence.
*   Experience with machine learning or AI systems.
*   Contributions to open-source projects.

### What We Offer

*   Competitive salary and equity.
*   Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.
*   401(k) with company match.
*   Flexible PTO policy.
*   A collaborative and inclusive work environment.
*   Opportunities for professional growth and development.

